    "q-107023": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107023",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ of polynomials from $R[t],$ where\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=4t-8{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=-5t+10{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}\\cdot {p}_{2}(t)=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ not both zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=0.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the given expressions for ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t)$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(4t-8{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(-5t+10{t}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ (4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2})t+(-8{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation is true for every $t$ if and only if \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -8{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot column is the $1$st one. Hence, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the $1$st equation, we get\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{4}{x}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, for any ${x}_{2}\\ne 0,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}=\\frac{(\\frac{5}{4}{x}_{2})}{{x}_{2}}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
