    "q-107026": {
      "dom_id": "step-q107026",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B,C},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{3}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}10 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} & 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1} & -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8{x}_{2} & 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -5{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}10{x}_{3} & -3{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+10{x}_{3} & 3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} & -{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+10{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}/2 \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd. Hence, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. \n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $2$nd equation, we get ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substitute it into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}+5{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n$[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.$\n\nFinally, for any ${x}_{3}\\ne 0,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{3}}=\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{3}}=1.\n$$",
